        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>In the video game, when an environment target reduces a hero to 0 hp while Unforgiving Wasteland is in play, the player is given a choice of whether or not to remove the hero from play. &nbsp;The explanation for this behavior is the ruling that when multiple &quot;would be destroyed&quot; effects are triggered, the player is allowed to choose which applies. &nbsp;However, in this situation there are not multiple &quot;would be destroyed&quot; effects. &nbsp;Unforgiving Wasteland is the only &quot;would be destroyed&quot; effect. &nbsp;The hero incapacitation rule is an &quot;is destroyed&quot; effect.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">If the ruling also applied to cases with a &quot;would be destroyed&quot; effect and an &quot;is destroyed&quot; effect, then players should also be allowed to choose whether or not to resolve the effect of Ammo Drop before Unforgiving Wasteland removed a villain target from play, or whether or not to use Bee Bot&#39;s effect to destroy Unforgiving Wasteland before its effect could resolve. &nbsp;But, players are not given these options, meaning that the behavior is inconsistent.</span></p>",
